Q: How can I check whether a string contains only digits in Go? A: <p><code>strconv.Atoi</code> may not be the right tool here because it will fail on a long string of digits that represent a number that's larger than the maximum int, and it will accept a string that looks like <code>+123</code> or <code>-123</code>, which contain non-digit characters. If you just want to answer that exact question, does my string only contain the digits 0-9, regardless of the length of the string, looping is your best option (there's quite a bit of overhead with the regular expression method).</p>
<p>You could use something like this:</p>
<pre><code>func isdigit(s string) bool {
    if s == &quot;&quot; {
        return false
    }

    for _, c := range s {
        if c &lt; '0' || c &gt; '9' {
            return false
        }
    }

    return true
}
</code></pre>
